WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:02.802
-We're back with Wanda Sykes,
everybody.

00:00:02.802 --> 00:00:08.675
You have a new scripted podcast
with my dear friend Colin Jost,

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:11.044
"Trust Fall."
This is ten episodes on Audible.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:13.146
Your first scripted podcast,
I'm going to assume.

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.614
Did you enjoy it?
-I loved it.

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.716
-That's really fun.
-Yeah, it was a lot of fun.

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:21.387
You know, because it's like
how when you do a --

00:00:21.387 --> 00:00:24.423
you know, the animated movies
and stuff like that,

00:00:24.423 --> 00:00:27.727
it takes forever for them,
you know, to actually see it,

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.128
to actually see it.
-Right, yeah.

00:00:29.128 --> 00:00:31.764
-So this is so cool because
you go in, boom, boom, boom.

00:00:31.764 --> 00:00:33.632
-The next thing you know,
it's out there for the world.

00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:35.068
-Yeah.
-You play somebody

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.769
who's catfishing Colin Jost
is that --

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:40.506
I would say, of all my friends,
most likely to be catfished,

00:00:40.506 --> 00:00:42.408
-It's him.
-Just in real life. Yeah.

00:00:42.408 --> 00:00:43.576
-Yeah, yeah.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:44.978
-I think he'd still land
on his feet

00:00:44.978 --> 00:00:46.746
and it would all be fine,
but he does --

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.748
He's a very, like,
trusting soul.

00:00:48.748 --> 00:00:52.117
-Yeah, he has that faith,
that gullible -- trust--

00:00:52.117 --> 00:00:54.587
Okay. We'll go with trusting.
Yeah. Gullible.

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.922
-Gullible works.
-Yeah.

00:00:55.922 --> 00:00:58.191
-I feel like if you
professionally catfished people,

00:00:58.191 --> 00:01:00.260
you would see Jost.
Even if you were watching "SNL,"

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.495
you'd be like, oh, him for sure.
-Yeah. Right.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:05.698
Yeah, absolutely. You would drop
what you were doing and go,

00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.734
"Oh, wait a minute.
This guy." Yeah, yeah.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:11.037
-You would, like, mid catfish,
you'd be like, "I got to go.

00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:15.408
I'm also not who I said I was.
I got to go catfish that guy."

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.243
-[ Laughs ]
-This is very exciting.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:20.212
"Curb Your Enthusiasm" is
coming back for another season.

00:01:20.212 --> 00:01:21.714
You've been fantastic
on that show

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.316
over the years.
-Okay.

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:25.251
-Did you have --
Was that a part you had

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:26.453
to audition for, for them?

00:01:26.453 --> 00:01:30.256
-Okay, they tricked me
into auditioning.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:32.158
-They tricked you.
So maybe you could be catfished.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.160
-I hate auditioning.
-Okay.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.463
-I don't like to audition.
For one, I stink at it.

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:38.965
Yeah, it's not like
I think I'm good.

00:01:38.965 --> 00:01:40.366
-I'm really bad.
I was really bad.

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:43.469
-No, I've had -- I've been in,
like, a casting session

00:01:43.469 --> 00:01:46.505
and had papers, like,
snatched out of my hand.

00:01:46.505 --> 00:01:48.774
Like, we don't even want you
to have the script anymore.

00:01:48.774 --> 00:01:51.077
-Wow.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:53.112
I'm not good
at auditioning, but --

00:01:53.112 --> 00:01:56.849
So a friend of mine, she was
producing "Curb" at the time,

00:01:56.849 --> 00:02:00.086
and she said, "Look, I really
want to get you on this show."

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:01.521
You know, I said,
"Well, you know,

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:02.822
I'm not going to audition."
She said, "Okay, well, don't.

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.089
Just come by me, Larry.

00:02:04.089 --> 00:02:08.093
We're shooting down
at a car dealership today.

00:02:08.093 --> 00:02:09.528
Come by and you can meet them."

00:02:09.528 --> 00:02:11.163
I said, okay.
So I get down there

00:02:11.163 --> 00:02:14.400
and I walk in, and I'm like,
there's a lot of black women

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.669
buying Toyotas today.
Why?

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.507
This is weird.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:24.010
So then she said, "Wanda,
come on in," right?

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.445
So I go and I meet him,
and we're just talking.

00:02:26.445 --> 00:02:29.882
He goes, "Okay,
so you're out walking and --

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:32.685
and I'm just going to say,
hey, I know that tush anywhere."

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:33.987
And I was like,
"Why the hell would you say

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.488
something like that to me?"

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.757
And he's like, yep,
she's got the job.

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:39.458
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:40.826
-So that wasn't really
an audition.

00:02:40.826 --> 00:02:42.328
You just had to be Wanda Sykes.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.096
-Yeah, yeah.
-So that's very helpful.

00:02:44.096 --> 00:02:45.431
Well, it's a good fit.
and I will say, like,

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.266
that is --
I respect his process.

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:49.134
He knows exactly
how to get the right thing.

00:02:49.134 --> 00:02:50.470
And it's a great show

00:02:50.470 --> 00:02:52.772
because everybody's just
a natural version of themselves.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:53.973
-Right.
-You also have "The Upshaws"

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:55.875
coming back.
That's really exciting as well.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:59.945
This is a show that is really
exciting and means a lot to you.

00:02:59.945 --> 00:03:01.313
-It does.
Yeah.

00:03:01.313 --> 00:03:05.384
The show with Mike Epps
and Kim Fields, and yeah,

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:09.488
it's you know, it's a good old
throwback multi-cam

00:03:09.488 --> 00:03:12.225
about a working class family.
And I love doing it.

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:15.227
And I love that, you know,
we're coming back. So, yeah.

00:03:15.227 --> 00:03:16.629
-Well, congratulations on that.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:18.164
Congratulations
on the podcast.

00:03:18.164 --> 00:03:19.732
So wonderful
to see you as always.

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:21.701
-Thank you.
-You guys, that's Wanda Sykes.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.269
Everybody,
"Trust Fall"

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:25.104
is available
on November 30th on audible.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:26.739
We'll be right back
with Taran Killam.

